agent-ops task task-8e85f3de-01b0-40e0-b200-cd449f6b0d34: run land: land delivered subset of a stopped native run
intent: Add agent-ops run land <run-id> [--task <id>...] --yes. Preconditions: run paused|blocked|budget-limited, no live worker, run root exists; landing marker in run state blocks resume/respond/land (RUN_LANDING_IN_PROGRESS), stale when its pid is dead. Selection: unlanded delivered tasks, or --task subset whose dependencies are within selection or already landed (else RUN_LAND_DEPENDENCY_OPEN). Proof: separate landing session worktree from target; programmatic landing root without criteria advisory (L1 legacy criterion on config required verifiers, L2 review-only subset coherence), surface copied from run root; integrateSessionChildren with explicit run child worktrees; runAdvanceCommand verify + two-round tree review + finish with keepChildren so run child worktrees are pinned but never removed. After success: landed tasks stay delivered, run stays paused, landings[] + RUN_PARTIAL_LANDED recorded; later resume and finalize work unchanged (advance rebases, root re-verified, landed merges no-op). Failure: target unchanged, marker cleared, landings unchanged, landing worktree kept and rebuilt by next land.
criteria:
- land-happy-path: tests/run/land.test.ts: paused run fixture with delivered independent A and B and blocked C; parsed `run land <id> --yes` through runRunCommand returns RUN_LANDED whose text names A, B, the receipt path and `agent-ops run resume <id>`; target contains exactly A and B commits; persisted run status stays paused, A and B keep run task status delivered, landings[] records the receipt and an RUN_PARTIAL_LANDED event exists; task status of the run root task reports active and child worktree HEADs are unchanged; parsing `run land <id>` without --yes fails CLI_OPTION_NOT_ALLOWED
- land-closure: tests/run/land.test.ts: --task A with A and B delivered lands only A; --task B where B depends on unlanded A returns RUN_LAND_DEPENDENCY_OPEN; after A was landed earlier, --task B succeeds; --task with an id that is not a task of the run returns RUN_LAND_TASK_INVALID; a run with no delivered tasks, or whose delivered tasks are all in landings[], returns RUN_LAND_NOTHING; every refusal leaves target ref and run state unchanged
- land-exclusion: tests/run/land.test.ts: land on an active or awaiting-input run, or on a paused run with a live worker, returns RUN_LAND_STATE_INVALID; blocked and budget-limited runs are accepted; while a landing marker of a live process exists resume, respond and land return RUN_LANDING_IN_PROGRESS; a marker left by a process that no longer exists does not lock out the next land
- land-failure-atomic: tests/run/land.test.ts: two separate cases, conflicting delivered children (WORKTREE_INTEGRATION_CONFLICT) and a failing candidate verification, each leave the target ref unchanged, clear the marker, keep landings[] unchanged and keep the landing worktree; the next land removes and rebuilds the kept landing worktree; a landing worktree recorded for another run is refused with RUN_LAND_WORKTREE_FOREIGN and left untouched
- land-then-finalize: tests/run/land.test.ts: after a partial landing, RunService.resume of the run succeeds; delivering the remaining child and running the run finalize advance path finishes with a receipt, and the target history contains each delivered child commit exactly once
